00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:12.140
Well, we've reached the end of 2019 and once again we get to look back on another year of anime.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:16.900
We got to see all kinds of shows in all shapes and forms, so that begs the question:

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.620
What are you gonna remember 2019 for?

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.360
2019 has somehow equaled or maybe even eclipsed the monster year that was 2018.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.600
Anime is good now, it's just good,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.540
and with more of it than ever before. we have not been struggling for choices.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.980
We've had the good, the bad, the ugly, and just the plain weird,

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.180
so as we take a look back at what we watched, and probably what we missed,

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.540
let's see how anime signed itself off for this decade.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:50.560
This is...

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.520
Anime in 2019.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.780
I'm gonna be honest with you,

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.880
even I had trouble keeping up with all the anime coming out last year,

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.380
and I feel that's just kind of the norm nowadays.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:04.320
So instead of trying to cover everything, I'm just gonna keep it to my personal favorite things,

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.260
ending it on my anime of the year.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:10.620
But I'll do my best to talk about everything that mattered to me and made waves in our community,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.100
and looking back for a place to start in 2019,

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:17.960
there was one thing we kept having to ask ourselves over and over again.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.880
Are you excited for more isekai next season?

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.280
"No, hehehehe, no not another one."

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:25.140
"You're joking, not another one!"

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.120
One of these days, I'll get to look back on a year of anime and think to myself,

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:28.740
"Man,

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.540
there was a reasonably conservative amount of isekai this time."

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:32.620
This year wasn't one of them.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:36.080
Somehow the number doesn't seem to be decreasing but increasing.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.740
Every time, I say to myself,

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:41.020
"Surely we can't get even more isekai next year."

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:42.320
No. That is a trap.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:43.180
Don't say it.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:46.360
As soon as you do, some unsuspecting victim tries to cross the road

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:49.900
and truck-kun claims another life and nobody can stop it.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.160
So I'm just gonna stop doing it.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.700
I'm not going to think about it.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.400
I'm just not going to say it anymore.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.100
Alright?

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.700
And this isn't even a dig at the genre,

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:01.800
this year we saw more variation than the usual power fantasy affair that we're used to.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.480
Cautious Hero,

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:03.200
Kemono Michi,

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.540
and Ascendance of a Bookworm

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.540
all look genuinely good and different.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:09.860
I kind of just hit my isekai quota and haven't gotten around to watching them yet.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.040
But there were a lot of others I did enjoy.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.820
Shield Hero kicked off the year proving that all it takes to make a community collectively

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.460
forget about years worth of built-up isekai fatigue

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:22.080
was one raccoon girl and an angry boy.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.540
The series sported easily the most hatable villain of the year, that built up to a climax

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.680
*clapping*
so satisfying the only thing that was actually rising was the revenge boner that could be felt community-wide.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.020
so satisfying the only thing that was actually rising was the revenge boner that could be felt community-wide.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:31.920
*more clapping*
so satisfying the only thing that was actually rising was the revenge boner that could be felt community-wide.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.940
My only real problem was with how cheaply Naofumi was built up

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.120
by essentially bringing everyone else down.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.780
Sure you're rooting for Naofumi, but he's held up as being the only competent character

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.360
by making everyone but him and his party an absolute fucking useless idiot.

