But unlike previous years, there weren't any soundtracks as a whole that really stood out.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:42.440
That is of course until I realized the best anime music of the year was stuck behind Netflix jail.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:46.900
One of them was Beastars, but the other one gives me the opportunity to talk about..

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.900
♫ The Loneliest Girl - Carole &amp; Tuesday
(Vo. Nai Br.XX &amp; Celeina Ann) ♫

00:05:54.780 --> 00:06:00.060
Carole and Tuesday didn't just give us an OST, it just straight-up gave us several albums worth of music.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:04.480
The sheer amount of songs on display here in all different genres is absolutely insane.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:08.660
You've got stuff like EDM, metal, Carole and Tuesday's simpler acoustic sound,

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:12.100
whatever genre this fits into, and of course classic pop.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.700
And all that was just a single episode.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:17.100
While in most music anime, the show will normally centre around some musicians

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.060
building up to their next big performance, their next big song,

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.980
which if we're lucky will happen maybe every three [or] four episodes,

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:27.460
Carole and Tuesday is just here casually debuting at least one new song every episode.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:29.360
At least, one.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:33.540
Most of the time we're getting two, three or four, coming from the various characters on display,

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:36.100
not forgetting other miscellaneous things, like,
I don't know,

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.020
actual background music,

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:39.640
the OP's, the ED's,

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:43.000
and even references to the classical music of its setting in the future.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.880
Random character: "My mother passed away not that long ago."

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:49.680
"I'm singing a song she often sang to me when I was young."

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:52.180
*EXTREMLY deep breath*

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:54.180
T/N: Sounds that can only be described as jaw-dropping

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.060
I don't think there's been another anime that's come close to the amount of music in this show,

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:04.220
and I realize when watching this how much of a core element music is in all of Shinichiro Watanabe's works.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:08.940
Because this entire show felt like his personal love letter to music itself.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:13.720
And I don't think anyone else would have been able to get so many talented artists from all over the world

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:16.600
to help provide the music for a single anime.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:20.560
If the writing had been tighter, this had the potential to be an absolute masterpiece.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:26.440
But, as it stands it is simply a GOOD show with by far the most impressive music production

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:28.120
any anime has ever seen,

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:29.920
and maybe will ever get.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:33.880
'Cause I don't man, I don't see how any show will ever top the likes of this.

