00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.000
like another certain Brotherhood...

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:01.800
People are terrified right now at the implication of the World War Season 3 teaser that just got released,

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:06.640
forgetting that Quintessential Quintuplets has already started World War 5 in 2019,

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:09.140
and many of us have already been drafted.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:11.240
Senko-san was ASMR for the eyes,

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:14.900
by giving us a middle-aged salaryman mastering the forbidden technique of

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.120
DUAL WIELDING HEAD PATS

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.920
against some innocent boomer lolis

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:21.460
in what my depression has categorized as an Avengers level threat.

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:24.300
But if I had to talk about the shows that really had an effect on me,

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:27.220
the first one that comes to mind would have to be Kaguya-sama...

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:29.840
♫ Love Dramatic - Mayasaki Suzuki feat. Rikka Ihara ♫
Gigguk: Oh love me mister ♪

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:31.560
♪ Hey mister ♪

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:35.580
In one of the most refreshing takes of the romantic comedy genre I've seen in a while.

00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:40.220
The mix of the absurd, over-the-top mind games in the typical harem romance situations

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:43.860
was a premise that continued to be hilarious throughout, and before I knew it,

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:47.420
I was actually heavily invested in these two characters getting together.

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:49.860
I think there was another reason to watch a show, but um,

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:50.400
*clicks tongue* uhhh,

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.320
I just can't remember what it was right now...

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:59.160
*Chika noises synced to Beethoven*
♫ Ode to Joy - Beethoven ♫

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:00.960
Ah of course, how could I forget.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:02.420
Ishigami best girl.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:03.960
*Chika squeal*

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:07.480
O Maidens in Your Savage Season was probably my overlooked gem of the year

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:11.540
in one of the most hilariously accurate portrayals of puberty I've seen in anime.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:15.900
It's rare that you get to see the topic of sex tackled as the awkward, uncomfortable mess that it is

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:18.580
when you first discovered it and started thinking about it.

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:22.240
You know that one embarrassing sex story everyone seems to have as a teenager

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:25.730
that is hilarious to tell but kind of makes you want to die inside when you remember it?

00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:26.860
That is it.

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:27.800
That is the show.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:31.760
How Heavy Are the Dumbbells You Lift? finally gave us cute girls do lifting

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:33.800
in an anime so alpha not even tyler1 can come close to even matching it.

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:34.560
*scream*
in an anime so alpha not even tyler1 can come close to even matching it.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:35.240
in an anime so alpha not even tyler1 can come close to even matching it.

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:35.880
*macho noises*
in an anime so alpha not even tyler1 can come close to even matching it.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:38.200
*macho noises*

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:39.660
*Chika squeal*

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:41.720
While this might not be the greatest anime of the year,

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:44.380
it certainly had one of the biggest real-life effects on me,

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:48.420
because I don't want to admit that I'm THAT degenerate weeb who got motivated to join a gym

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:51.260
'cause I saw some cute anime girls doing it, but...

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:52.140
*sigh*

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:56.940
I'm that degenerate weeb who got motivated to join the gym because I saw some cute anime girls doing it,

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.060
which makes me think,

00:12:58.060 --> 00:12:59.880
"What's next for cute anime girls?"

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.120
Cute girls do basic daily hygiene?

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:04.420
Cute girls do filling out your annual tax return?

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:07.160
Cute girls do interacting with cute girls in real life?

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:11.600
Whatever it is, I think we finally figured out the end goal of all moe shows:

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:15.100
Cute girls do transforming weebs into functional members of society.

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:19.080
And then, there was my personal favorite high school drama of the year.

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:21.080
I came in to Beastars knowing nothing,

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:22.860
ready to meme the shit out of it,

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:25.740
and I came out with one of my favorite anime of the year.

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:28.620
This feels like one of the most unique series in recent memory,

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:32.060
and no, it's not because the characters are walking furry baits.

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:34.640
This doesn't feel like your typical glossy anime.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:36.960
In fact, it doesn't feel like anime at all.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:41.420
It gives off the vibe of an Oscar-nominated film or a highly acclaimed stage play,

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:45.200
with the combination of some of the best voice acting performances you can find all year,

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:49.400
and fantastic direction that was one of the only times in my life that had me saying,

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:50.020
"Man..."

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.980
"I'm really glad this anime's in 3D."

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:54.680
It's the story of a murder mystery,

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.320
an unequal society dominated by the strong,

00:13:57.320 --> 00:14:00.980
a man driven to obsession to be THE image of the perfect star,

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.960
and also a touching love story between

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:04.960
a literal virgin and actual chad.

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:09.240
The world of Beastars is one that draws you in and sells you on these characters.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:15.540
It deeply immerses you, then sells you on pure drama and emotion.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.540
[Legosi beating the shit out of him]

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:26.780
[Oh shit]

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:33.420
It says a lot that a show about anthropomorphized animals was the one that felt most real.

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:37.980
You forget that you're watching wolves, rabbits, deers, and Metal Gear Panda.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:42.420
In fact, their animalistic characteristics are able to emphasize emotion in a way

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:44.560
that makes them seem even more eerily...

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:46.160
human.

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:50.700
And I can't wait to see what the story will have to offer in season 2 and hopefully beyond.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:54.600
Basically, in a nutshell, I watched Beastars, and I'm still not a furry...

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:57.740
BUUUUUU-

00:14:57.740 --> 00:14:58.560
*clicks tongue* No.

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:00.400
Well...

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:08.500
Normally in the year of anime we get to see some high-octane, hard-hitting shows.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:10.160
So with that in mind,

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:11.980
what did 2019 offer us?

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:13.980
♫ Roller Mobster - Carpenter Brut ♫

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.060
Yeah, this year was kind of dry as a whole.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:25.180
For real though, 2019 was one of THE MOST action-packed years in recent memory,

00:15:25.180 --> 00:15:28.380
with old and new franchises not only continuing the expected hype,

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:31.220
but a lot of the times reaching their absolute peak.

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:34.040
Demon Slayer blew up the entire community in a single episode,

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:37.740
Mob Psycho 100 showcased some of the most impressive fight sequences I've ever seen,

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:43.280
Attack on Titan topped IMDB's chart for the highest-rated episode of any series of all time,

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:45.860
and My Hero Academia did an excellent job at

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:47.220
coloring in some manga panels.

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:50.900
(They totally made up for it later though.)

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:55.000
There are several anime of the year contenders right here, and most of them could have easily won

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:58.640
if they had aired in any other year, so this is going to be a pretty long segment.

00:15:58.640 --> 00:15:59.540
Let's start with Mob.

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:02.920
The first season of Mob always felt like it was living in the shadow of One Punch Man,

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:07.280
but this was the season it truly grew into its own, and maybe even surpassed its older cousin.

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:09.120
What I expected was more great action,

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:10.980
more great animation like the first season,

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:13.180
and it delivered that, then exceeded it.

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:16.740
Fight after fight after amazing fight, it was an absolute spectacle,

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:21.160
with the group battle against the teleporting psychic being one of the coolest sequences I've ever seen.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:24.200
But what I didn't expect was how much heart it would have as well.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:27.080
The character writing between Mob and Reigen was phenomenal,

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:30.600
and the unexpected character development they saw, and teary moments in the season,

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:33.180
sucker-punched me way harder than any of the fights.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:37.420
It grew from this flashy, funny action series to something so much more.

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:39.880
It was hype. It was emotional. It was touching.

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:41.880
It was just the complete package.

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:45.720
After it finished, I didn't think anything could come close to Mob this year,

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:47.900
and then Attack on Titan must have heard that and was like,

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:48.440
"Yo..."

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:49.980
"Hold my kidnapped Eren."

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:50.700
Attack on Titan

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:51.320
Attack on Titan Season 3

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:51.860
Attack on Titan Season 3 Part 2

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:52.580
Attack on Titan Season 3 Part 2 Half-Life 3

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:53.820
Attack on Titan Season 3 Part 2 Half-Life 3
Platform 9 3/4

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:57.420
was the perfect payoff to everything the series had been building up so far.

00:16:57.420 --> 00:17:02.700
The legacy of one of the most hyped franchises to rise up in the past decade had finally reached that hype,

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.360
then punched straight past it.

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:08.440
Seeing the evolution of the series go from thrill ride to mystery to political thriller

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:12.080
to the culmination of all of this was an absolute joy to experience.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:16.780
The mixture of a fully developed cast we were all invested in being put into a high-stakes situation,

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:19.840
where you genuinely did not know what was going to happen,

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:24.100
resulted in a dramatic, tense, action-packed,
edge-of-your-seat experience

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:27.960
that delivered some of the most compelling entertainment you can find anywhere this year,

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:29.100
anime or not.

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:32.280
It's also one of the few series that has built up this massive mystery,

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.960
and actually delivered a satisfying answer.

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:40.300
From what I've heard, the events of Season 4 are going to surpass even this, so I am absolutely hyped.

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:45.460
I cannot wait to properly experience it for the first time over the coming year the only way I know how to:

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:45.960
through

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:49.040
dipshit manga readers who can't resist posting spoilers in the comments section.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:53.560
And then Vinland Saga finally broke the curse of a highly-acclaimed, historical seinen manga

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:56.120
getting an actual decent anime adaptation.

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:59.480
I originally thought that if Vinland Saga were to ever get an anime,

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:02.880
all it would need to do is to animate the manga in a competent fashion,

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:04.860
and it would be a contender for anime of the year,

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:07.360
and that's exactly what happened.

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:09.780
The tale of viking Sasuke on his lone quest to

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:10.720
OK BOOMER

00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:12.180
everything his dad tried to teach him

00:18:12.180 --> 00:18:15.100
and Aske-chad trying to set the world record for longest

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:20.480
father-killing kill streak in history is one that will stick with me for a very long time.

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:23.800
While it may not be as loud or in-your-face as some of the other shows here,

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:26.820
it hits just as hard or maybe even more so.

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:32.700
This is gonna go down as a special series and with the ending it gave, it was the perfect way to cap off the year.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:36.280
My Hero Academia has pretty much continued being
My Hero Academia.

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:38.740
Me and the boys continued our trip across Italy in

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:41.480
(Google translate's American accent)
JoJo's Bizarre Adventure Golden Wind

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:45.280
(Google translates poor excuse of an Italian accent)
JoJo's Bizarre Adventure Golden Wind

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:46.060
♫ Funiculì, Funiculà - Luigi Denza ♫

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:52.980
Yes, JoJo Part 5 continued in a season where Italy itself became a JoJo reference,

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:56.440
as anime watchers finally understood the pain of the question,

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.880
(African accent)
"How the fuck does King Crimson work?"

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:02.020
Fans were finally rewarded with many highly anticipated moments

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:05.620
including the animated seven page muda that was a glorious moment

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.480
(Dio's sad yet proud wryyy in the background)
any father would be proud of.

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:08.240
Next up is

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:08.740
*Cocking gun SFX*
Meg: "Oh my god the fire's got a gun!"

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:10.240
Meg: "Oh my god the fire's got a gun!"

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:10.980
*Bang*
*Bang*

00:19:11.720 --> 00:19:12.220
*Bang*

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:14.840
Louis: "What the fuck was that?"

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:17.040
♫ Inferno - Mrs. Green Apple ♫

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:21.080
Fire Force took the phrase "Fighting fire with fire" to whole new heights

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:25.640
as David Production finally got a chance to flex their animation muscles outside of JoJo,

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:29.700
giving us a show with several choices of amazing top tier waifus

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:30.560
and Tamaki.

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.060
Yeah I said it, Tamaki fans.

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:32.840
What are you gonna do?

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:33.940
Trip over and land on my dick?

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:36.320
Look, I'm a degenerate that lives for trashy fanservice,

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:39.280
but there's a time and a place for that and I don't need it breaking all the immersion

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:41.460
of every serious action scene she's in.

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:45.740
Finally, of course, there was Demon Slayer, which was undoubtedly the new breakout hit this year.

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:49.740
I can't remember the last time I saw such an instant explosion from just a single episode.

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:52.440
See, there was Demon Slayer before episode 19

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:55.460
and then there was Demon Slayer AFTER episode 19.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:59.860
It went from this moderately popular action show to the hip trending topic on Twitter.

00:19:59.860 --> 00:20:04.460
Everyone started watching it, and then Ninja tweeted that it was gonna become the greatest anime of all time

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:05.460
and everyone was like,

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:07.540
"Well, I mean, he's pretty good at Fortnite."

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:08.920
"So he's probably right."

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:09.420
*Frolic begins playing*

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:14.440
Not to take anything away from the scene, as I do think it was one of the most beautifully crafted moments

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:15.880
I've seen in any shown in any shounen.

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:17.540
I mean I kind of called it a work of art.

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:20.980
And it is a really good show but I think as a whole it's a bit premature,

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:24.460
because the story only just feels like it's truly started to get going,

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:28.160
and its competition this year are shows that have reached their narrative peaks.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:32.780
What I find more interesting is how after all these years we've kind of got a big three again.

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:34.380
With One Piece staying where it is,

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:36.480
Naruto being replaced by green Naruto,

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:40.900
some people could even argue that Demon Slayer has just filled that gap for the new generation's Bleach.

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:41.400
*clears throat*

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:41.900
*clicks tongue*

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:44.860
But I'm not gonna be the one to start that shitstorm of a conversation.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:48.700
Before I get to my anime of the year,

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:51.720
there are a few more shows that didn't really belong to any of these categories

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:53.600
but definitely shouldn't be left out.

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:56.800
Promised Neverland was an engrossing thriller about a group of children

00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:59.640
breaking out of an extremely secure locked down facility,

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:02.040
overlooked by highly intelligent monsters...

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:03.560
by playing tag.

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:06.420
This was some of the most gripping anime you could find this year.

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:08.480
Aside from having a completely unique premise,

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:12.180
the cat-and-mouse game manages to deliver a story with so many twists and turns

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:14.280
without ever feeling like they were forcing it.

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:17.520
It builds up tension beautifully and it's one of those cliffhanger shows that will have you

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:18.940
clicking on the next episode

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:20.120
faster than you could say

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:21.800
ITADAKIMAAASU!!

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:22.420
Gordon: "Finally,"

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:23.980
"some good fucking food."

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:28.720
If I had any small issues with it, is that it pushed my suspension of disbelief to the fucking limit.

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:30.420
Like I know these kids are meant to be smart,

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:33.580
but when they started playing 5D intergalactic mind games

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:36.280
and had already strategized their highly elaborate escape plan

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:38.080
from the moment they were fucking conceived,

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:40.030
all while masking it as a children's game,

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:40.720
I was like,

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:43.340
"I don't know if these kids could be going THAT far."

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:47.180
♫ Moon Men (Instrumental) - Jake Chudnow ♫
Or can they?

00:21:47.180 --> 00:21:51.080
And if we're still nitpicking, there something a bit off about how the characters were drawn,

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:53.760
but I couldn't quite put my finger on it.

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:55.740
"Did he just say there was something off about the way we look?"

00:21:55.740 --> 00:21:57.200
"Yeah, I think he did just say that."

00:21:57.200 --> 00:21:59.680
"I don't think there's anything weird about my face. I have a normal face!"

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:01.080
"No, you look perfectly normal."

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:01.980
"What do you think Ray?"

00:22:01.980 --> 00:22:03.940
"Yeah, I have no idea what the hell he's talking about."

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:06.600
Meanwhile, in Dr. Stone character designs...

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:10.800
(Radio static communication)
"Suffix zero six, we are approaching runway one-niner are we clear to land? Over."

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:15.740
"Suffix zero six, you are number one for runway one-niner, you are clear to land whenever you are ready. Over."

00:22:15.740 --> 00:22:18.580
"Suffix zero six, thank you very much, taking it down now."

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:20.580
*Airplane approaches runway*

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:25.200
*Airplane has now landed*

00:22:27.100 --> 00:22:28.040
It's time

00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:29.620
to d-d-d-d-d-d-d-d-

00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:32.660
Dr. Stone this year gave us a long-awaited anime adaptation of

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:36.800
those two Indian guys building huts on YouTube that somehow got recommended to you at 1 a.m.

00:22:36.800 --> 00:22:39.960
And I'll be honest, this show left me a bit conflicted in the end.

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:42.660
On one hand, it's one of the most interesting premises out there,

00:22:42.660 --> 00:22:46.420
and seeing the process of how they make advanced technology with the most primitive of tools

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:49.460
was some of the most entertaining things you can find in anime all year.

00:22:49.460 --> 00:22:50.940
But on the other hand,

00:22:50.940 --> 00:22:54.200
I could give less a shit about any of the conflicts here.

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:56.380
Look, I really don't care that Tsukasa hates boomers.

00:22:56.380 --> 00:22:59.100
Anytime there was a contractually obligated Shounen Jump fight,

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:01.580
I couldn't help but just wanna go back to seeing the villagers

00:23:01.580 --> 00:23:04.160
pissing themselves at the sight of Senku making glass.

00:23:04.160 --> 00:23:08.180
It's probably the first time in my life when I've seen a tournament arc and I've been like,

00:23:08.180 --> 00:23:08.680
"Oh."

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:10.520
"They're putting in a tournament arc."

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:12.820
*yaaawwwwnn*

00:23:12.820 --> 00:23:13.400
*That sound you make when you wake up while drooling*

00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:13.960
"Yeah,"

00:23:14.260 --> 00:23:16.260
"wake me up when something interesting happen-"

00:23:16.260 --> 00:23:16.760
*Awe-inspired gasp*

00:23:16.760 --> 00:23:18.140
"LIGHHHT BULLB

00:23:18.140 --> 00:23:20.500
AAAAARRRRRRRR--"

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:24.920
No Guns Life almost single-handedly tried keeping the cyberpunk genre alive along with Psycho-Pass,

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:29.560
giving us an old-school hard-boiled detective story that unfortunately got looked over by a lot of people,

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.760
probably because its name wasn't something hip and catchy enough like,

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:35.680
That Time Alphonse Elric Got Reincarnated As A Gun.

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:39.000
Dororo was a legitimately good remake of a samurai anime from the 60s

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:41.980
that hardly anyone watched because it was an Amazon Prime exclusive,

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:45.440
and the only way I see people still remembering the show is when they ask Amazon,

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:46.420
"Hey Amazon."

00:23:46.420 --> 00:23:48.220
"Do you have Demon Slayer on Amazon Prime?"

00:23:48.220 --> 00:23:49.060
and Amazon's like,

00:23:49.060 --> 00:23:51.720
"Oh, yeah, we have Demon Slayer on Amazon Prime"

00:23:51.720 --> 00:23:53.800
and this is their Demon Slayer on Amazon Prime.

00:23:53.800 --> 00:23:57.860
Hoshiai no Sora was a really promising anime original sports drama whose production just got

00:23:57.860 --> 00:24:00.560
axed halfway through leaving us once again with just

00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:01.460
half an anime.

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:04.540
Fate is still making more money than they know how to spend.

00:24:04.540 --> 00:24:06.740
Babylon was a great show that I apparently missed.

00:24:06.740 --> 00:24:07.240
Umm.

00:24:07.240 --> 00:24:07.820
*weird gasp*

00:24:07.820 --> 00:24:09.700
Let's see. Was there anything else I left out?

00:24:09.700 --> 00:24:11.820
*A sound I don't want to hear again or ever describe*

00:24:12.320 --> 00:24:12.920
*A sexual ass moan*

00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:15.480
Yeah, I think that's everything.

00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:25.260
This year was honestly the hardest year to pick my anime of the year for a very long time.

00:24:25.260 --> 00:24:30.540
I praise 2018 for the sheer volume of good shows but, 2019 has seemingly matched that

00:24:30.540 --> 00:24:35.800
while still producing a handful of shows that were even better than anything that came out the year before.

00:24:35.800 --> 00:24:40.140
Many of these shows would have been an easy shoo-in if they literally aired in any other year.

00:24:40.140 --> 00:24:41.440
It was a tough choice,

00:24:41.440 --> 00:24:44.000
but after dwelling on it for a week or two,

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:44.940
I've got to give it to...

00:24:44.940 --> 00:24:46.860
*Drumroll*
I've got to give it to...

00:24:46.860 --> 00:24:47.760
*Drumroll*

00:24:47.760 --> 00:24:48.740
Vinland Saga.

00:24:48.740 --> 00:24:53.560
I've said previously that every so often you come across a work of fiction like Vinland Saga,

00:24:53.560 --> 00:24:57.800
something that exudes this sense of unquantifiable greatness,

00:24:57.800 --> 00:25:01.500
and there is a word that personifies what I'm talking about...

00:25:02.160 --> 00:25:03.440
a masterpiece.

00:25:03.440 --> 00:25:08.020
To me, Vinland Saga is a tale that earnestly earns that title.

00:25:08.020 --> 00:25:10.020
Mob might have been better animated,

00:25:10.020 --> 00:25:12.040
Attack on Titan might have been more compelling,

00:25:12.040 --> 00:25:14.040
Demon Slayer might have been more hype,

00:25:14.040 --> 00:25:15.780
Beastars might have been more unique,

00:25:15.780 --> 00:25:20.560
but I know the tale told in Vinland Saga will stick with me for much longer.

00:25:20.560 --> 00:25:25.000
I mean, it already has, this isn't the first time I've got to experience this story,

00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:28.100
but that didn't make it hit any less hard.

00:25:28.100 --> 00:25:30.760
It's a story that's powerful and raw,

00:25:30.760 --> 00:25:32.040
brutal and grim,

00:25:32.040 --> 00:25:33.940
yet, somehow it's...

00:25:34.220 --> 00:25:35.080
beautiful.

00:25:35.080 --> 00:25:39.060
Culminating in one of the greatest climaxes anime has ever seen.

00:25:39.060 --> 00:25:44.140
The series displays some of the best character writing and developments you could find in its diverse cast,

00:25:44.140 --> 00:25:47.340
but even so there was still one clear standout,

00:25:47.340 --> 00:25:50.580
because 2019 was the year of Askeladd.

00:25:50.580 --> 00:25:53.260
Askeladd isn't just the antagonist of the year.

00:25:53.260 --> 00:25:57.980
Askeladd is the character of the year and a contender for the whole decade.

00:25:57.980 --> 00:26:01.160
It's not often you come across this multifaceted character,

00:26:01.160 --> 00:26:05.820
who is not only compelling to watch but commands your attention every second he's on screen,

00:26:05.820 --> 00:26:09.380
exuding the type of charisma that doesn't just charm the people in the story,

00:26:09.380 --> 00:26:10.780
but yourself as well.

00:26:10.780 --> 00:26:13.420
It says a lot that a character you end up cheering for,

00:26:13.420 --> 00:26:14.580
laughing for,

00:26:14.580 --> 00:26:15.540
crying for,

00:26:15.540 --> 00:26:17.980
is this manipulative scheming bastard

00:26:17.980 --> 00:26:20.660
who is responsible for killing hundreds of people,

00:26:20.660 --> 00:26:21.840
innocent or not,

00:26:21.840 --> 00:26:25.180
and personally ruined God knows how many more lives.

00:26:25.180 --> 00:26:29.080
Every fiber of your being tells you that you should hate this man

00:26:29.080 --> 00:26:31.480
and you end up just loving him.

00:26:31.480 --> 00:26:33.340
Some people try living as a hero,

00:26:33.340 --> 00:26:35.740
only to see themselves becoming the villain.

00:26:35.740 --> 00:26:38.900
But, here was a man who chose to live as the villain

00:26:38.920 --> 00:26:40.400
who we all saw

00:26:40.400 --> 00:26:41.240
became...

00:26:41.680 --> 00:26:42.320
a hero.

00:26:43.260 --> 00:26:46.360
This was the final series I finished before the year ended

00:26:46.360 --> 00:26:50.900
and I can't think of a better way to cap off a fantastic year

00:26:51.300 --> 00:26:52.180
for anime.

00:26:53.160 --> 00:26:53.720
*Giorno's theme kicks in*

00:26:53.720 --> 00:26:56.340
So as 2020 now has fully come,

00:26:56.340 --> 00:26:57.620
one last time,

00:26:57.620 --> 00:26:58.580
let's give it up

00:26:59.060 --> 00:27:00.060
for 2019.

